## 2.2.git helper · local@unix
rc=0
git-credential-keyrack: no readable @all.camp.GITHUB_TOKEN — declines
  ⚠️ this message CANNOT name the cause, and must not pretend to.
     the get above is run with stderr discarded, because git must never
     see keyrack's chatter on a decline path. so what reached here is one
     empty string, and at least four different faults produce it.

  ⇒ ask the box, which CAN tell them apart:
      rhx git.grove.send <grove> --play diagnose.grove-github-credential
    or run the same get by hand, with its stderr kept:
      cd <fixture> && rhx keyrack get --owner ehmpath --key GITHUB_TOKEN \
        --org @all --env camp --unlock --allow-dangerous --value

  the four it will be, and the fix for each — measured 2026-08-06:
    locked 🔒   the session lapsed (540m). a re-unlock is the whole fix:
                  rhx keyrack unlock --owner ehmpath --env camp
    errored 💥  the aws.params vault cannot load its peers. fix at cause:
                  rhx grove.provision --what 5.3.brains --mode apply
    absent 🫧   no value was ever stored. a set is the fix:
                  cd <fixture> && rhx keyrack set --owner ehmpath \
                    --key GITHUB_TOKEN --org @all --env camp --vault os.secure
                  (answer BOTH prompts at a tty; never pipe them)
    refused     the value is there and github rejects it — mint a fresh
                pat, then re-set the same slug

  ⚠️ the pat needs scope 'repo' to serve this helper. 'read:org' is a
     SEPARATE capability that serves gh's discovery, not the clone

